# .gitignore
# ──────────
# Generated data artifacts (large, and exactly reproducible from SEED=42 in
# data/generator.py — so the recipe is committed instead of the output).
data/raw/*.csv
data/processed/*.csv

# Trained model binaries. Regenerate with `python -m models.train`.
models/saved_models/*.xgb
models/saved_models/*.bin
models/saved_models/*.pkl

# ── DELIBERATELY NOT IGNORED: models/saved_models/metrics.json ──
# It is generated, so the instinct is to ignore it. Don't. It is the published
# evidence for every number in the README, and the dashboard and API read it,
# so a clone without it cannot show a single metric.
#
# The reason committing it is safe is that staleness is now *guarded*: v2
# shipped a metrics.json advertising ROC-AUC 0.9999 for a model that had already
# been retired, and nothing caught it. tests/test_baselines.py::
# TestMetricsAreNotStale::test_metrics_describe_the_current_model_version fails
# the build the moment the file's model_version drifts from features.MODEL_VERSION,
# and a second test recomputes the leakage claim against the shipped CSVs. Keep
# both if you keep the file committed.

# pyvis writes its bundled vis-network/tom-select JS beside any saved HTML.
# Vendored third-party assets, regenerated on every dashboard run.
lib/

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.egg-info/
dist/
build/

# Test / tooling caches
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/

# Virtual environments
venv/
.venv/
env/

# IDE
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo

# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Streamlit
.streamlit/

# Jupyter
.ipynb_checkpoints/
